 "title": "London, 21 April 1506: the princess's household and the greed of certain persons",
 "caption": "Lines 24-27 of De Puebla's letter to Almazán, AGS Patronato Real leg. 54 doc. 78, deciphered sign by sign with Tomokiyo's reconstruction of Puebla's First Cipher (decode.py). Clear words of the letter are shown in plain type.",
 "unit": "signs",
 "key_note": "Puebla's First Cipher: one sign per letter, with second signs for a, i and u/v (Tomokiyo's reconstruction of Bergenroth's key no. 6); the Roman-numeral group is a code word of Puebla's Great Roman Numeral code. The groups are shown by the ASCII names the transcription gives the drawn signs (46 = the '46'-shaped sign, + = the cross, Q = the crossed L). The value of the Roman-numeral group is taken from the key in AGS PTR leg. 52 doc. 33 and its C-count was not checked on this letter. Word division is editorial.",
